In article <24881@hacgate.SCG.HAC.COM>, root@lyra.scg.hac.com (Dave Fisher) writes:
> 
> Is there a method to find out a vaxes hardware ethernet address(es) 
> through a software utility or command?
> 
-- 

There is an undocumented command to SDA that will show you the physical and
hardware address of your ethernet.  Use the commands:

	$ ANALYZE /SYSTEM
	SDA> SHOW LAN /FULL

... about three screens down you will find both ethernet addresses.

Another way is in NCP.

	$ RUN SYS$SYSTEM:NCP
	NCP> SHOW KNOWN LINE CHAR
	NCP> SHOW EXEC STATUS

... also shows both addresses.

LATCP (if you have LAT running) will show you the hardware address with
the command:

	$ MCR LATCP SHOW LINK /FULL

Some VAX hardware allows you to display the physical address from the three
angle bracket prompt.  I'm at home now and don't remember the exact command.
It is something like ">>> SHOW ETHERNET"  or is contained in ">>> SHOW ALL".
Consult the hardware documentation for your specific system.

Hope this helps,
-Bob Longo

