There was one other problem:  DEC's penchant for overpricing hardware
components.  

Many years ago -- I forget when, but I do remember that it was during the 
glory days of AT-class machines with EGA video -- I priced out a very 
nicely-equipped PC-based Fortran platform for an engineer.  And just for grins,
I looked at a Pro-380 solution too.  

