specified a Micropolis 1335 -- which is, as many of us know, essentially the
same drive used by DEC as the RD53. 

The complete AT-based system, with 1 MB RAM, 12 MHz 80286, 80287 math
co-processor, EGA display card and monitor, 70 MB disk, miscellaneous hardware
like keyboard and serial ports and such, plus MS-DOS and Microsoft Fortran, 
came to just about what DEC was charging for the RD53!!!  

YES, this has been fixed to some extent in DEC's current price book.  However,
DEC has a *lot* of history of bad vibes to overcome. 

