|>The executable *DOES* work, but we would like to find a way to modify this
|>linker behavior. It looks as though the qualifier /SELECTIVE_SEARCH 
|>on the LIBRARIAN command would do it, but no permutations I have tried 
|>with this qualifier have eliminated the error. Can anyone out there 
|>advise me as to correct usage of this qualifier to eliminate these error
|>msgs? They make debugging a link of a large piece of software sheer h*ll, 
|>as we have ended  up with as many as 93 undefined symbols, when possibly 
|>only a very few are really needed or valid.
|>

This isn't the linker or the librarian, it's the compiler.  On VAX, the
Fortran compiler puts out a separate object module definition for each
routine; to the librarian, linker, it looks as if each routine is in its
own module.  On AXP, the compiler, by default, compiles all the routines in
a source file into one module.  This is why when one routine is extracted, the
other comes with it.

If you want the VAX behavior, compile with the /SEPARATE_COMPILATION
qualifier.  See the DEC Fortran for OpenVMS AXP User Manual for more details.
