In article <24881@hacgate.SCG.HAC.COM> fisher@lyra.hac.com (Dave Fisher) writes:
>
>Is there a method to find out a vaxes hardware ethernet address(es) 
>through a software utility or command?

If you are lucky, you can get the hardware ethernet address using the 
uerf(8) command.  The system startup messages report the address.

    loy jgealow % uerf -c oper | fgrep hard

Take a look at your hardware manual.  If you are lucky, there may be an 
easy way to get the address using a console command.

On a VAXstation II/GPX, you can get the hardware address using the 
following sequence of console commands:

    >> e/p/w 20001920
    >> e
    >> e
    >> e
    >> e

Each command will yield a number which ends with FF##.  Concatenate the 
##s to get a 10-character address.

Jeff Gealow



