In article <1993Jan25.085406.23877@ugle.unit.no>, venaas@swix.nvg.unit.no (Stig Venaas) writes:
>We've got a MicroVax II and two VaxStation 3200 which
>are in terrible need of more diskspace.
>
>What kind of disks can they use?
>
>We have some SCSI and some standard PC MFM disks. Is it
>possible to connect any of those? I guess not though.


They take ST-506 MFM drives. The RD54 is a Maxtor drive; the RD53 is a
micropolis. Non-standard drives (i.e. non-DEC equivalent geometries) will
also work; the uVAX will detect that it doesn't recognize it and ask for
the geometry. I'm not sure what this actually looks like, as I've never
done it.

To format a drive, enter a "T 50" ot "T 51" at the console prompt.
One of these is a drive verification, the other is a format (I get them
mixed up as to which is which).

