Fortunately enough for me, most of you out there in netland realized, I was 
posting an opinion and not a fact.  Having "Stupidly" deleted my .signature 
file, my disclaimer was no where to be found.

Some things I think that need to be said.

1) I didn't mean to imply that I or DEC thought users were stupid.  I meant
to imply (and most people picked up on this) that in my opinion, DEC was
just being extremely cautious by not having patches available.  I personally
feel that we need to do something to get the fixes out in a reasonable,
timely, and efficient matter that solves customer's problems and doesn't
cost DEC an arm and a leg.  Posting them on the internet is one
solution.

2) I think that instead of discussing it here, we should do something about it.
I propose the following: Send me a mail message (since I've already marked
most of the news messages as read, and came into this discussion in the
middle,) containing the following information:

	Why DEC should post patches on the internet.
