EtherNet HW address in a primitve licensing scheme to ensure you only run their
stuff on the one machine you bought it for. By retaining the address chip, you
can still run the software on the new machine. (You might still be breaking
the licence agreement, though, if it also is capacity based.)

Does this make sense ? Any comments ??

