callahan@vax.oxford.ac.uk writes:

>I have a problem setting up DNS on a network of Suns running SunOS 4.1.1
>and DECstations running Ultrix v4.2a.  These share a single YP domain
>and there are servers among both the Suns and the DEC machines.

>The problem is setting up the Sun clients to use DNS.  As I understand
>it (and as I have done before), I should tell ypserv to issue DNS
>requests on behalf of its clients by giving the -b option to makedbm
>in the YP makefile.

>The catch is that when the Sun clients start up, some of them at least
>end up getting bound to a DEC machine.  Now, the Ultrix YP software doesn't
>know how to do DNS lookups, since in the DEC scheme the clients do
>this themselves.  The net result (so to speak!) is that some Sun clients
>don't get DNS service.

>What can I do? 

I have just finished almost exactly the same setup: 2 of SUN10/SunOS 4.1.3
and 4 of DEC5000/Ultrix4.3.
The solution is to run the YP and DNS master and slave servers on the SUN.
In this way all DEC and SUN ypbind bind to the SUN and SUN get the right
YP->DNS mapping.
The other way is to upgrade your SUN to Solaris 2.x and you will get the
right DNS/YP operation.

(Sun should be sued for damages caused by this YP/DNS fuckup).

-- 
Peter Ziobrzynski, pz@modtor.uucp, peter@sni.ca, Toronto, Ont. Canada


