In article <1993Jan20.173831.21087@iscnvx.lmsc.lockheed.com>, burkhardt@skynet.ssd.lmsc.lockheed.com writes...
>Hello!  I need to know if anyone is running a LAVC cluster over a T1
>link?  If so could you please tell me about your experiences.  If possible,
>perhaps send me a phone number so that we can have a more interactive
>dialogue.
> 

We tried this once just to see how it well it worked.  We had assumed that we
would have to increase some of the cluster related timing parameters, but found
that it actually worked with all the parameters set to their default values.  We
had a small LAVC (about 6 nodes) at the time, and could detect no performance
impact, but we only had MV II and 2000, a real CPU might notice the difference.
We were confident that DEC would never support it, but I had heard their
engineers state that in principal cluster could run over any transport,
depending on what kind of performance impact you are willing to take.

