I use the PFM performance meter.  The following is the release notes from
the author.  I do not know what the current release is but perhaps he can
give you information.



	Performance Meter Utility for DECWindows V2.0

	(c) 1989 by Robert Heller

	This utility displays performance indicators in a small DECWindows
window.  Included in the display is CPU busy, processor modes, and disk I/O
statistics on the system device (SYS$SYSDEVICE) and a "local" disk (defined
by the logical PFM$LOCALDISK).

	Differences from version V1.0:  Added paging statistics (faults,
paging I/O, free page count, modified page count). Minor adjustments in
placements of various widgets.

	Differences from version V1.1:  Added changes suggested by Mark
Pizzolato - INFO COMM Computer Consulting, Redwood City, Ca,
mark@infopiz.UUCP or uunet!lupine!infopiz!mark:
	- Compaction of the Modes Display to save window real estate.
	- Respacing of the Counter Titles to allow user specified titles
		(via logical names PFM$DEVICE_n_TITLE)
	- Allowed up to 4 User Selected Devices to Monitor, selected by
		defining PFM$DEVICE_n_NAME and PFM$DEVICE_n_TITLE
	- Smoothed out the Counter Updates to remove the delayed flicker.
	And fixed the X graphics contexts to use GXinvert instead of GXcopy,
to allow display visibity of reverse-background display setups (Suggested by
Christopher Ho <chris%skat.usc.edu@usc.EDU>).


