We have recently installed a Vaxstation 4000/90 and installed a DEC RZ25,
a Fuji M2654, Fuji M2652 and Fuji M2266 SCSI drives.  Everything worked
fine until the disks began to have a load put on them (we're using the
4000 as a LAVC server) at which time we started to log errors on both
the SCSI controller and all disks but the M2266.  

The typical error messages on the controller comprised
- unexpected interrupt
- arbitration failed
- bus reset initiated

Typically, the drives would report a fatal controller error, go offline
and quickly come back on.  However, if they happened to be in the middle
of a write operation, the file would end up with a bad bucket.

Neither DEC nor Fujitsu has an definitive answer at this time.  DEC switched
out the 4000 motherboard but that didn't solve the problem so it would 
appear not to be a faulty SCSI controller.  The Fujitsu drives are all happily
working off a MV3100 SCSI controller, so they wouldn't seem to be the
problem.  DEC "suspects" there may be a compatibility problem with having
the RZ25 and the Fuji drives on the same controller.  Fuji "suspects" the
2654 & 2652 are too fast for the 4000 controller (even though they're both
supposed to be SCSI 2) and suggests we slow the drives down...

Anyone seen a similar problem?  thanks very much...


