In article <1993Jan15.152636.580@hhcs.gov.au>, pihlab@hhcs.gov.au writes:

> Additional information about TA-90 backup problem:
> 
> The *.ISM files are RMS Index files and it appears that the last few blocks
> in the file get verification errors.
> 
> Perhaps this part of the file has not been used yet but why would it give me
> the verification errors?  Data should be just copied and compared.

There's a known bug in BACKUP when you use /VERIFY on an indexed file on a
disk that has high-water marking enabled.  Workarounds are (if I recall all
of them correctly):  Ignore the error messages; remove /VERIFY; turn off high-
water marking on those volumes.

This problem might be fixed in V5.5-2 or in a CSC patch -- I remember it being 
mentioned somewhere, but can't recall if it is, indeed, fixed.

There's a DSNlink article describing this behavior.  Check DSNlink or call the
CSC to get a copy of the DSNlink article.

