... and here it is:

$ PATCH YFDRIVER                                        ! 16/1/92/dcs
!
! THIS IS A PATCH FOR V5.3-1 SYSTEMS ONLY!  See below for details on how to
!                                           modify it for other versions.
!
! This patches YFDRIVER to allow the 38400 bits per second speed to be set
! on a DHV11.  REMEMBER TO TAKE A COPY OF THE DRIVER BEFORE RUNNING IT.
!
! The DHV11's ports are split into pairs of ports 0 & 1, 2 & 3 and so-on.
! The speeds supported by the DHV11 are split into two groups (A & B), with
! most common speeds supported in both groups.  However, each port in a pair
! must both be supported in the same group.
!
! All the speeds supported by the unpatched YFDRIVER are in group B, so this
! problem doesn't arise.  However, 38400 is a group A speed only, and therefore
! the other port in a pair must be set to a speed that is supported in group
! A.  If you set a port to 38400 and the other port is in a group-B-only
! speed, it will be changed to a group A speed (or something odd).
!
! The group B speeds not supported in group A are:
!
!       Speed           Corresponding group A speed
!          75              50
!         150             200 *
!        1800            7200
!        2000            1050 *
!       19200           38400
!
! * These speeds are not defined group A speeds, and can only be selected
! by making a group B to group A switch via the other port in the pair.
!
! The value of 1DD (hex) for YF$VMS_SPEEDS is correct for VMS V5.3-1.  You may
! need to adjust this value for other versions of VMS.  The tables look like:
