L309
Monday
March 29
AUTOGEN:  How to Use it, What it Does for You, and What it Will Do to 
You
  
AUTOGEN is designed to make systems management easier.  Most of the 
time it does.  But, once in a while, AUTOGEN appears not to help!  It 
also provides useful knowledge to programmers who use any method of 
interprocess communications, since most communication of this nature 
can require the adjustment of SYSBOOT parameters, hopefully done with 
AUTOGEN. 

This seminar first acquaints you with AUTOGEN and how to successfully 
use it.  Then it delves into the command procedure itself.  We look at 
what SYSBOOT parameters AUTOGEN adjusts and what relationships it 
tries to enforce between the different parameters.  We also look at 
how AUTOGEN decides what images should be INSTALLed at boot time and 
how it sizes your paging and swap files.  AUTOGEN works differently in 
the different versions of AUTOGEN, as they exist now and in the near 
future.  We look at those times when AUTOGEN is not the right tool to 
use and what should be done then.  Finally, we discuss AUTOTUNING - 
the wave of the future. 

Topics covered include:
~ What is AUTOGEN?
~ How Do You Normally Use it?
~ What Work Does AUTOGEN Assume that You Have Done?
~ What Must You Do to Make it Work Right?
~ What Other Support Tools Can You Use?
~ What SYSBOOT Parameters Will it Help You Adjust?
~ What Other SYSBOOT Parameters Will it Adjust for You?
~ How Does it Decide What to Adjust?
~ How Much Does it Adjust Things?
~ Why Does it Adjust Things That Way?
~ When Might it Make Invalid Decisions?
~ How Will You Fix Things Up When it Doesn't?
~ How Does AUTOGEN Decide What Images Should Be INSTALLed?
~ How Does it Decide What Size to Make the System Files?
