There have been some Q-bus multiplexors (from Emulex and possibly others)
that support 38.4K when the OS sets the speed to some little-used value
like 2000 baud.  Bear in mind, though, the the VMS terminal driver doesn't
have terrific throughput, and you probably can't support streaming 38.4 K
on an MVII.

The fact that the VMS driver doesn't support RTS/CTS handshaking is another
drawback to high-speed transfers.  The WorldBlazer will do XON/XOFF, but
somewhat less efficiently.

I see (looking back) that I'm assuming that you're using VMS.  If you're
using UNIX, your mileage may vary.

